import * as cdk from "aws-cdk-lib";
import * as s3 from "aws-cdk-lib/aws-s3";
import * as cloudfront from "aws-cdk-lib/aws-cloudfront";

findings.recommendation:
Replace S3_MANAGED encryption with KMS encryption:

const logBucket = new s3.Bucket(this, "AccessLogBucket", {
  bucketName: `disruptionai-frontend-logs-${this.account}`,
  encryptionKey: new kms.Key(this, "LogBucketKey", {
    enableKeyRotation: true,
    description: "Encryption key for CloudFront access logs",
  }),
  blockPublicAccess: s3.BlockPublicAccess.BLOCK_ALL,
  removalPolicy: cdk.RemovalPolicy.DESTROY,
  autoDeleteObjects: true,
  objectOwnership: s3.ObjectOwnership.OBJECT_WRITER,
  lifecycleRules: [{ expiration: cdk.Duration.days(90) }],
});

Replace S3_MANAGED encryption with KMS encryption:

const siteBucket = new s3.Bucket(this, "SiteBucket", {
  bucketName: `disruptionai-frontend-${this.account}`,
  encryptionKey: new kms.Key(this, "SiteBucketKey", {
    enableKeyRotation: true,
    description: "Encryption key for frontend assets",
  }),
  blockPublicAccess: s3.BlockPublicAccess.BLOCK_ALL,
  versioned: true,
  removalPolicy: cdk.RemovalPolicy.DESTROY,
  autoDeleteObjects: true,
});

If the Lambda only posts to connections from the same API Gateway, the current scope is acceptable. If further restriction is needed, document that the wildcard is required for the Lambda to post to any active WebSocket connection. Add a comment:

// Wildcard required: Lambda must post to any active WebSocket connection
resources: [
  `arn:aws:execute-api:${this.region}:${this.account}:${api.ref}/*`,
],

This is acceptable as it only logs keys (metadata), not values. However, consider adding a comment to clarify this is intentional:
```typescript
// Log UI data structure (keys only, no values)
logger.info("Streaming", `UI data from envelope: ${Object.keys(uiData).join(", ")}`);
```

Rename the Pydantic model class from 'ManpowerAvailability' to 'WorkforceAvailability'. Update all imports and usages:

from constraint_matching_agent.models.schemas import (
